# Build dispatcher tick (sd:6098; design:
# docs/work/2026-10-24-build-dispatcher/design.md). Each tick writes the
# build-dispatch heartbeat, reaps lost runs, watches the lane for enqueued
# runs, claims a bundle under the builder caps, and spawns one supervisor
# per run that has none. No model runs in the tick; a supervisor runs the
# builder, its review and its enqueue, or a draft run's read-only spec
# (sd:6013).
#
# Run it on the hub and on each satellite that hosts a lane: each tick
# acts on its own host's lanes only (sd:7932). Install it in that
# machine's `<config>/cron-jobs/jobs/<host>/`. Run logs go under its
# pack config's `sd.bulk_storage_root`; on a satellite name a local
# system-disk folder there, not the NAS (sd:6705).
#
# JOB_TIMEOUT bounds the tick: it reads the gate load, the lane list and
# the database, and stats the bulk storage root for run logs. A hung
# volume there held every tick to this limit for 12 hours (sd:6705);
# until the pack bounds that probe (pack sd:6749), a run of rc=124 lines
# here points at the volume first; after three in a row the breaker
# skips slots and probes every 30 minutes (sd:6831). A supervisor
# starts in a new session with the job's lock closed
# (`start_new_session`, `close_fds`),
# so neither this limit nor the next slot reaches it; it bounds its own
# builder at 60 minutes. A slot that finds the previous tick still active
# logs `skipped` and exits 0.
#
# SD_PACK_ROOT is escaped so the `bash -c` that runs the command reads it,
# after ~/.config/shell/env.sh; this file is sourced before env.sh is.
# env.sh also exports CUSTOM_CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, which a supervisor
# hands to its builder's environment alone.
JOB_SCHEDULE="*/2 * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="90s"
JOB_COMMAND="\"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow}/bin/sd\" assignments dispatch"
